. They also apply to the following groups if the University requests proof of their English proficiency:\nNew Zealand Residence Class visa holders\nPermanent residents of New Zealand or Australia\nDiplomats or consular officials living in New Zealand, and their dependents.\nIf English requirements differ for these groups, they are marked \u201cDomestic student status\u201d in the programme-specific information.\nFind out about English language criteria for your study\nUse the links below to find out how to meet the English language requirements for your study plans:\nGroup 1: Standard undergraduate English requirements\nBachelor's degrees (for exceptions, see Group 4)\nUndergraduate Study Abroad and Exchange programmes\nFind out the requirements for Group 1\nGroup 2: Standard postgraduate English requirements\nHonours year of a Bachelor\u2019s degree\nGraduate Certificate and Diploma (for exceptions, see Group 4)\nPostgraduate Certificate and Diploma\nMaster\u2019s degree (for exceptions, see Group 3 and 4)\nPhD studies (for exceptions, see Group 3)\nPostgraduate Study Abroad and Exchange programmes\nFind out the requirements Group 2\nGroup 3: Higher English language requirements\nMaster of Laws\nPhD in Law\nPhD in Education\nPhD in Linguistics/Applied Linguistics\nFind out the requirements for Group 3\nGroup 4: Programmes with external English requirements\nBachelor of Midwifery\nBachelor of Education (Teaching) Early Childhood\nGraduate Diploma of Teaching (Early Childhood Education/Primary/Secondary)\nMaster of Teaching and Learning (Primary/Secondary)\nMaster of Nursing Practice.\nFind out the requirements for Group 4\nRelated links\nEntry requirements\nConnect with us\nContact us\nFind an agent\nInformation sessions\nGet a student guide\nEmergencies\nFaculties\nArchitecture and Design Innovation\nBusiness and Government\nEducation, Health, and Psychological Sciences\nGraduate Research\nHumanities and Social Sciences\nLaw\nScience and Engineering\nContacts and d